    "st10.date": {
      "doc": "ST-10",
      "quote": "October 28, 2026\nFederal Reserve issues FOMC statement"
    },
    "st10.vote": {
      "doc": "ST-10",
      "quote": "The Federal Open Market Committee approved the following statement for release by a 10 – 2 vote:"
    },
    "st10.hold": {
      "doc": "ST-10",
      "quote": "The Committee decided to maintain the target range for the federal funds rate at 3-3/4 to 4 percent"
    },
    "st10.econ": {
      "doc": "ST-10",
      "quote": "Economic activity is expanding at a strong pace."
    },
    "st10.infl": {
      "doc": "ST-10",
      "quote": "Inflation remains elevated."
    },
    "st10.more": {
      "doc": "ST-10",
      "quote": "The accumulation of more information will help the Committee determine the policy stance appropriate to ensure a timely return of inflation to the Committee's 2 percent goal."
    },
    "st10.dissent": {
      "doc": "ST-10",
      "quote": "Voting against the monetary policy action were Lisa D. Cook and Beth M. Hammack, who preferred to raise the target range for the federal funds rate by 1/4 percentage point at this meeting."
    },
    "pc10.six": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "Americans, of course, are still dealing with inflation that has been running above\nthe Committee’s objective for close to 6 years."
    },
    "pc10.cond": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "Since our policy action in September, we have started to see some changes in financial\nand credit conditions. They have tightened for some businesses and households, much as we\nwould expect."
    },
    "pc10.nottight": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "And while overall financial conditions are tighter, I’m unwilling and unable to call\nthem tight."
    },
    "pc10.energy": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "But inflation is too high.\nEnergy and related prices have moved higher again in recent weeks."
    },
    "pc10.why": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "So why not just raise rates today?"
    },
    "pc10.calendar": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "quashing inflation is not about some fixed individual date on a calendar."
    },
    "pc10.acted": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "And so in September when we last met, we acted. We removed a dose\nof accommodation."
    },
    "pc10.notyet": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "you haven't delivered yet, you\nhaven't achieved price stability, you're right about that. But we're working on it."
    },
    "pc10.work": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "overwhelming judgment is that what we've done in this monetary medicine is starting to work\nsome, but there's no firm conclusions."
    },
    "pc10.clarity": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "take stock of where we are, evaluate what we're seeing out the window, ask ourselves\nwhether the period right in front of us is likely to provide more clarity on the appropriate\nprotocol. My judgment, the judgment of my overwhelming number of colleagues is that it would."
    },
    "pc10.means": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "dominant means in which this policy is going to be put into practice is we are tightening\nfinancial conditions. They've tightened a bit since we met last time. That isn't something that\nwe're uncomfortable with. That tells me that policy is working"
    },
    "pc10.dots18": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "I don't submit a dot. I don't plan on\nsubmitting a dot, but the 18 of them do."
    },
    "pc10.noprejudge": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "I also don't believe in prejudging meetings. A lot of things can\nhappen. So I'm not going to be able to share with you my musings about what happens when this\ngroup gets together six weeks from now."
    },
    "pc10.sched": {
      "doc": "PC-10",
      "quote": "2027, one meeting will focus exclusively on broad monetary policy strategy, with neither a vote\non the federal funds rate nor a policy statement anticipated."
    },
    "cook.date": {
      "doc": "SP-COOK-0928",
      "quote": "September 28, 2026\nAn Update on AI and the Economy\nGovernor Lisa D. Cook"
    },
    "cook.long": {
      "doc": "SP-COOK-0928",
      "quote": "This increase was to address inflation, which has been too high for too long."
    },
    "cook.pressure": {
